     :k :md/in-file,
     :v #uuid "acc0a0bd-8c52-3f95-a05a-02e836171807"}
    {:e #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e",
     :k :md/heading,
     :v "Decisions of 14 October 2026 — order and time apart"}
    {:e #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e",
     :k :md/level,
     :v 2}
    {:e #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e",
     :k :md/text,
     :v
     "Sid made these on 14 October 2026, in chat, from a page of his refinements\nthat a session wrote at his word\n(`src/proposal/backend-on-rama-2026-10-02/order-and-time/REFINEMENTS.md`), and\nfrom a session's questions on it. Words in quotation marks with an id of the\nrecord are lines that he typed. Where he answered with a session's wording,\nit says so."}
    {:e #uuid "b70d9b24-4ece-34e2-9fb2-ca400183f7ca",
     :k :md/in,
     :v #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e"}
    {:e #uuid "b70d9b24-4ece-34e2-9fb2-ca400183f7ca",
     :k :md/number,
     :v 1}
    {:e #uuid "b70d9b24-4ece-34e2-9fb2-ca400183f7ca",
     :k :md/title,
     :v "Order and time are apart, and order never uses the time."}
    {:e #uuid "b70d9b24-4ece-34e2-9fb2-ca400183f7ca",
     :k :md/text,
     :v
     "1. **Order and time are apart, and order never uses the time.** His lines\n   (‹aa212e6b›): \"so we also make the order and time different is that what\n   you saying??? btw my intent was the same\"; (‹2f80019d›): \"so from what i\n   am understanding: order and time are different and we don't use the time\n   for ordering. every thing that goes in depot has a time attached to it\"; and, asked whether that was his\n   direction, (‹296a2a7b›): \"my intent was the same yes\". What comes with it:\n   - A stamp is the layer's count of decisions: the last stamp plus one, or 0\n     for the layer's first, for an accept and a refusal alike.\n   - The time on the act is a label. A gate writes it beside the stamp and no\n     rule reads it. The rule of 10 seconds on a carried stamp went with it,\n     and so did the bound of 2^45 on the time, whose one reason was the\n     time's place in the stamp. Of the four things that 13 October left not\n     decided, \"where a time that is far ahead is stopped\" fell away: a time\n     far ahead is a wrong label and nothing else.\n   - It replaces entry 4 of 8 October, his answer \"clock-time+counter\"\n     (‹f3f530b8›) to the sheet's H2 A, \"the wall time and a counter, in one\n     integer\". What it gives up: one number for \"as of 15:00\" in every\n     layer. A session's view, which he did not rule on: that can be built\n     later from the depots, which keep every act with its time and what it\n     is based on."}
    {:e #uuid "b70d9b24-4ece-34e2-9fb2-ca400183f7ca",
     :k :md/cites-sid,
     :v #{"296a2a7b" "2f80019d" "aa212e6b" "f3f530b8"}}
    {:e #uuid "b70d9b24-4ece-34e2-9fb2-ca400183f7ca",
     :k :md/cites-session,
     :v #{}}
    {:e #uuid "f233d6a2-bf7f-38bb-a620-eff233f32a64",
     :k :md/in,
     :v #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e"}
    {:e #uuid "f233d6a2-bf7f-38bb-a620-eff233f32a64",
     :k :md/number,
     :v 2}
    {:e #uuid "f233d6a2-bf7f-38bb-a620-eff233f32a64",
     :k :md/title,
     :v
     "An act's stamp is not raised above the stamps that it carries, and no check holds a carried stamp against the layer's last stamp."}
    {:e #uuid "f233d6a2-bf7f-38bb-a620-eff233f32a64",
     :k :md/text,
     :v
     "2. **An act's stamp is not raised above the stamps that it carries, and no\n   check holds a carried stamp against the layer's last stamp.** He answered\n   a session's two questions with that session's wording, \"Drop the jump\n   above carried stamps? Yes.\" and \"Keep the own-layer check? Leave it out:\n   one rule fewer, and it protects nothing\" (‹296a2a7b›; the words are those\n   of «6c16b53a»), and with his own (‹f6a39dde›): \"makes sense both of them\".\n   That an act came after what it is based on is read from its `:based-on`,\n   by fact id. No gate reads a carried stamp, so its bound of 2^62 went."}
    {:e #uuid "f233d6a2-bf7f-38bb-a620-eff233f32a64",
     :k :md/cites-sid,
     :v #{"296a2a7b" "f6a39dde"}}
    {:e #uuid "f233d6a2-bf7f-38bb-a620-eff233f32a64",
     :k :md/cites-session,
     :v #{"6c16b53a"}}
    {:e #uuid "2027a87a-5a9c-31d6-ad0f-5f1d9275bf49",
     :k :md/in,
     :v #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e"}
    {:e #uuid "2027a87a-5a9c-31d6-ad0f-5f1d9275bf49",
     :k :md/number,
     :v 3}
    {:e #uuid "2027a87a-5a9c-31d6-ad0f-5f1d9275bf49",
     :k :md/title,
     :v "The time is on the rows and on the answer."}
    {:e #uuid "2027a87a-5a9c-31d6-ad0f-5f1d9275bf49",
     :k :md/text,
     :v
     "3. **The time is on the rows and on the answer.** Asked whether the time goes\n   on each fact's row and on the answer, he answered \"1) yes\" (‹296a2a7b›). A\n   session's, for him to review: a read hands it when the query asks for it,\n   as it hands who wrote a fact; and a refused thing keeps its time in its\n   answer when it held a usable one."}
    {:e #uuid "2027a87a-5a9c-31d6-ad0f-5f1d9275bf49",
     :k :md/cites-sid,
     :v #{"296a2a7b"}}
    {:e #uuid "2027a87a-5a9c-31d6-ad0f-5f1d9275bf49",
     :k :md/cites-session,
     :v #{}}
    {:e #uuid "70bd27f6-2a6f-34ef-ad08-a950458c7971",
     :k :md/in,
     :v #uuid "bfbd279d-826d-3a46-aef9-04166110960e"}
    {:e #uuid "70bd27f6-2a6f-34ef-ad08-a950458c7971",
     :k :md/number,
     :v 4}
    {:e #uuid "70bd27f6-2a6f-34ef-ad08-a950458c7971",
     :k :md/title,
     :v "A thing that arrives with no time is refused."}
    {:e #uuid "70bd27f6-2a6f-34ef-ad08-a950458c7971",
     :k :md/text,
     :v
     "4. **A thing that arrives with no time is refused.** \"2) refuse\"\n   (‹296a2a7b›). It was built so on 13 October and kept for his word."}
